    "title": "Abortion is back on the Missouri ballot, but this lawsuit aims to stop a vote - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Hannah Falcon (KCTV5) ,\n5 hours ago JEFFERSON CITY, Mo. (KCTV) - A legal battle over the wording of a ballot question on abortion access is playing out in Cole County Court. Cole County Judge Daniel Richard Green heard arguments in the trial on Wednesday afternoon. The ACLU is representing a Missouri woman, Anna Fitz-James, suing the state over the wording in the question put on the ballot by Missouri state lawmakers. The ballot measure seeks to remove the abortion access put into the Missouri constitution by the passage of Amendment Three in November 2024. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak 34",
